  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">GenU Egypt (Shabab Balad) developed the foundation for a government-led multi-sectoral platform to support the transition of young people fromLearning to Earning. The Shabab Balad governance structure includes Shabab Balad Advisory Board that is responsible for the strategic direction of GenU Egypt and Shabab Balad Coolition with its 5 subcommittees where each represents a strategic pillar for Shabab Balad. The Government endorsed Shabab Balad as tool to achieve the Voluntarily National Commitment for Learning to Earning that aims &amp;ldquo;by year 2027, 13 million young people (46% of youth population) in Egypt are in secondary education, skilled and trained, decently employed or with entrepreneurship opportunity, digitally connected or positively engaged in their society&amp;rdquo;.The Shabab Balad Board endorsed GenU Academy to accelerate the achievement of the National Voluntarily Commitment. GenU Academy will have a Head Quarters in central Cairo with a plan to spread in different youth</narrative>
   </title>
